  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prev3C &#x2013; Prevention of Cervical Cancer in Cambodia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Prev3C will provide self-swab HPV testing to 1,000-1,800 women aged 30-49 years in hard-to-reach communities, to improve access to and uptake of CC prevention services. Malaria Consortium Cambodia (MC) is currently providing remote populations in Cambodia with malaria and CC services through the RAI4E programme and SHERCAN project, respectively. The SHERCAN project aims to increase awareness of CC and available services, and strengthen the health system to provide CC prevention services. Prev3C will be integrated with SHERCAN to provide HPV pre-screening which is not covered by the existing project. Women diagnosed with HPV as part of the Prev3C project will be referred for further screening at treatment provided.</narrative>
  </description>
